  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic constant-score loopback fixtures with 20 ms artificial HTTP delay, alternating paired trials on shared hardware; no universal latency, relevance, billing or token-cost claim.",
    "Linux is the existing ARM64 Docker VM, not independent native Linux hardware. Windows is cross-compiled only.",
    "Admission estimates decoded/encoded/provider scratch; it is not a process RSS cap. Retained pages, output, HTTP buffers and allocator overhead have separate bounds.",
    "Sustained-image memory and CPU improve, while warm elapsed time can increase. First-output and CPU do not improve uniformly.",
    "Warm asset downloads remain required. Generic server-authoritative conditional source projection and complete predicate certificates remain future contracts.",
    "Raw reports and logs are local ignored output, not published downloadable evidence.",
    "The integration suite uses the previously frozen native server binary; this implementation changes the CLI and shared evidence-loader ownership, not server query semantics."
  ],
